1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,770
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,770 --> 00:00:03,010
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:03,710 --> 00:00:06,310
Please take a look here.
We're looking for someone.

4
00:00:06,910 --> 00:00:08,450
Excuse me, please take a look.

5
00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:10,010
Please take a look at this.

6
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:11,380
(Episode 45)

7
00:00:11,650 --> 00:00:12,720
Here.

8
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:14,520
Please take a look.
We're looking for someone.

9
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:15,650
(Missing Person)

10
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:16,760
(Jeon Dam I, Age 5, Lost in 2002)

11
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:17,820
(Please Help Find Our Family.
Reward Offered)

12
00:00:17,820 --> 00:00:19,060
(Lost 24 Years Ago)

13
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,530
(Searching for Our Grandniece Dam I,
Age 5 in 2002)

14
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:24,800
Here, please.
I'm looking for someone.

15
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,660
- Please take a look.
- I'll visit the client myself,

16
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:28,200
- so why don't we grab a bite first?
- Please take a look.

17
00:00:28,630 --> 00:00:29,700
Da Mi, are you hungry?

18
00:00:29,930 --> 00:00:33,170
- Yes, to be honest, I'm starving.
- Working in our field,

19
00:00:33,170 --> 00:00:36,240
you'll often miss meal times.
You'll have to get used to it.

20
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:37,740
Okay.

21
00:00:38,340 --> 00:00:41,310
I'm starving too, Team Leader Cha.
What are we having?

22
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:44,120
Well, it's customary...

23
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:45,550
to let the newcomer
pick the lunch menu.

24
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:46,990
Da Mi, you choose.

25
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:48,150
What are you doing?

26
00:00:48,150 --> 00:00:50,390
- He said you pick the menu.
- Yes.

27
00:00:50,590 --> 00:00:51,690
Excuse me.

28
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:53,490
Please take a look at this.

29
00:00:53,490 --> 00:00:54,590
(Missing Person)

30
00:00:54,790 --> 00:00:55,990
I'm looking for someone.

31
00:00:56,130 --> 00:00:58,230
Yes. Just a moment.

32
00:00:58,660 --> 00:01:00,100
Kang Da Mi, hurry up.

33
00:01:00,330 --> 00:01:01,330
Yes, I'm coming.

34
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:05,340
Hey! Jeon Bok Sim?

35
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:07,740
(Missing Person)

36
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:10,580
Hey, stop right there!

37
00:01:10,910 --> 00:01:12,240
- Darn it.
- Oh, my gosh.

38
00:01:12,310 --> 00:01:13,310
Darn it.

39
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:16,780
What's their problem?

40
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:20,950
I told you to hurry up.

41
00:01:21,750 --> 00:01:23,820
Yes, Head Designer Cha. I'm sorry.

42
00:01:25,190 --> 00:01:26,190
Let's go.

43
00:01:32,530 --> 00:01:34,030
(Missing Person)

44
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:37,700
When are you going to pay us back,
handing out flyers like this?

45
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:39,140
Well? Bok Sim.

46
00:01:40,610 --> 00:01:42,110
Just sit back and watch.

47
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:43,480
If you want to get your money,
that is.

48
00:01:43,940 --> 00:01:45,440
(Missing Person)

49
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:47,950
What are you doing, Bok Sim?

50
00:01:49,310 --> 00:01:50,380
(Jeon Jin Sook)

51
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:51,420
(Missing Person)

52
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:53,180
Whatever.

53
00:01:53,590 --> 00:01:55,690
However she scrapes it together,

54
00:01:55,850 --> 00:01:57,890
we just need to get our cut.

55
00:01:57,890 --> 00:01:59,090
Right, boss?

56
00:02:01,230 --> 00:02:03,530
It's me. Did you get the photo?

57
00:02:03,660 --> 00:02:04,660
Did you take a good look?

58
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:06,100
Where are you right now?

59
00:02:07,130 --> 00:02:09,970
I took a picture of the flyers
I had left...

60
00:02:09,970 --> 00:02:11,400
after handing them out
in front of your office.

61
00:02:12,570 --> 00:02:15,370
I still have a whole stack left.

62
00:02:16,610 --> 00:02:18,780
I'm thinking of handing out the rest
when everyone leaves work.

63
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,480
Tell me what you want.

64
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:21,880
Just know that...

65
00:02:22,150 --> 00:02:24,580
pulling the same stunt
won't work anymore.

66
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:28,550
Twenty thousand dollars.
Just that much will do.

67
00:02:29,390 --> 00:02:31,060
You'll send it right now, won't you?

68
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:33,060
Hey, Jin Sook.

69
00:02:35,460 --> 00:02:36,900
(Missing Person)

70
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:38,660
(Missing Person,
Jeon Dam I, Age 5, Lost in 2002)

71
00:02:38,730 --> 00:02:41,300
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

72
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:43,800
I'm sick of this.

73
00:02:48,310 --> 00:02:51,010
(Complete transaction?
Depositing 20,000 dollars, complete)

74
00:02:53,750 --> 00:02:54,750
I sent it.

75
00:02:55,310 --> 00:02:58,080
Yes, I see it. That was fast.

76
00:02:58,380 --> 00:02:59,380
Thank you.

77
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:01,320
If you have...

78
00:03:02,150 --> 00:03:05,320
even an ounce of genuine gratitude
toward me,

79
00:03:06,620 --> 00:03:08,460
stop pulling
these ridiculous stunts...

80
00:03:09,830 --> 00:03:12,600
because my patience
has officially run out.

81
00:03:16,470 --> 00:03:17,800
I really need to get rid of her.

82
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:19,800
I will get rid of her.

83
00:03:22,340 --> 00:03:23,340
Wait.

84
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:26,740
How dare she hand out flyers
right in front of my company?

85
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:34,220
- Honey.
- Why are you so startled?

86
00:03:35,390 --> 00:03:36,850
Come on in, Mother.

87
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:41,130
Mother, you're here?

88
00:03:41,530 --> 00:03:42,530
Yes.

89
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:47,000
You should've let me know
in advance.

90
00:03:47,730 --> 00:03:48,800
Well.

91
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:51,670
I realized it's been so long
since all of us,

92
00:03:51,740 --> 00:03:53,910
including Mother and the kids,
had a meal together.

93
00:03:54,110 --> 00:03:55,710
That's why we came to have lunch.

94
00:03:56,610 --> 00:03:57,610
What?

95
00:03:57,880 --> 00:04:00,350
Are you displeased
that your mother-in-law...

96
00:04:00,450 --> 00:04:01,850
showed up unannounced?

97
00:04:01,910 --> 00:04:04,920
Why would you say that, Mother?
I'm glad you came.

98
00:04:05,420 --> 00:04:08,550
It's good for you to get out
for some fresh air like this.

99
00:04:09,290 --> 00:04:11,860
I'll tell Do Yun to bring Seung Yun
up to the office.

100
00:04:12,190 --> 00:04:15,830
I already called on the way,
but they'd already left.

101
00:04:16,930 --> 00:04:18,560
It's too bad we arrived a bit late.

102
00:04:18,830 --> 00:04:20,570
Let's just take Mother
and eat together.

103
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:21,900
All right, Mother.

104
00:04:24,970 --> 00:04:26,300
What are you in the mood for?

105
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:28,110
I'll treat you
to something delicious.

106
00:04:32,180 --> 00:04:33,180
No.

107
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:36,810
Goodness.

108
00:04:42,190 --> 00:04:44,820
Is this your office, ma'am?

109
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:49,560
It's nice. You decorated it well.

110
00:04:51,430 --> 00:04:54,600
Does this company
belong to you, ma'am?

111
00:04:55,270 --> 00:04:57,140
- Is it?
- What do we do?

112
00:04:58,900 --> 00:04:59,900
Mother.

113
00:05:00,510 --> 00:05:04,610
This is where your daughter-in-law
sits and works.

114
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:05,710
CEO Jeon.

115
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:08,150
You told her to be the CEO,
a long time ago.

116
00:05:08,710 --> 00:05:11,750
My daughter-in-law is dead.

117
00:05:12,450 --> 00:05:13,850
She died a long time ago.

118
00:05:14,420 --> 00:05:16,720
She's in a better place now.

119
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:22,330
I should call her.
I want to hear her voice.

120
00:05:22,590 --> 00:05:26,000
I'm going to ask her
why she won't take me with her.

121
00:05:26,330 --> 00:05:29,270
- No, Mother. Give that to me.
- I don't want to.

122
00:05:30,370 --> 00:05:33,540
I'll make the call for you,
Mother, okay?

123
00:05:33,910 --> 00:05:35,570
- What?
- Please give it to me.

124
00:05:58,360 --> 00:06:01,870
Mother. We came out to eat.

125
00:06:01,970 --> 00:06:03,530
Let's head out together now, okay?

126
00:06:04,570 --> 00:06:05,570
What?

127
00:06:07,670 --> 00:06:09,670
Why am I sitting here?

128
00:06:10,610 --> 00:06:13,380
Do Yun's mother, I'm sorry.

129
00:06:15,380 --> 00:06:16,580
It's all right, Mother.

130
00:06:17,980 --> 00:06:19,350
What? All right.

131
00:06:20,620 --> 00:06:22,520
- Let's go, honey.
- Okay.

132
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:23,820
Wait...

133
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:26,220
Why are you breaking out
in a cold sweat?

134
00:06:26,790 --> 00:06:27,990
Are you coming down with something?

135
00:06:28,390 --> 00:06:29,390
Me?

136
00:06:36,330 --> 00:06:37,340
Fortunately,

137
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:40,570
it seems I'm a much better actor
than you are.

138
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:46,780
Don't push yourself too hard,
Do Yun's mother.

139
00:06:47,180 --> 00:06:49,150
You'll make yourself sick.

140
00:06:50,820 --> 00:06:51,850
Yes, Mother.

141
00:06:52,250 --> 00:06:54,650
- I'm fine.
- Good.

142
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:04,830
This is the hospital schedule,

143
00:07:04,860 --> 00:07:06,230
outlining your upcoming
treatment plan.

144
00:07:08,630 --> 00:07:10,570
Please look it over
carefully at home...

145
00:07:10,840 --> 00:07:12,370
and consult with me first.

146
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:15,410
I'll help you, Ms. Jo.

147
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:19,940
When do I need to make
a decision by?

148
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:23,210
The sooner, the better,

149
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:25,950
but your own wishes
are what matter most,

150
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:28,720
so if you have any questions,
please call me anytime.

151
00:07:29,250 --> 00:07:31,160
Especially if coming in
feels like a burden.

152
00:07:32,790 --> 00:07:36,330
It looks like
you haven't told your family yet.

153
00:07:43,470 --> 00:07:45,400
Is there anything else on your mind?

154
00:07:51,810 --> 00:07:56,380
Feel free to ask me anything.
I'll do my best to answer.

155
00:07:59,250 --> 00:08:00,750
At the university hospital,

156
00:08:01,850 --> 00:08:03,820
I was all alone and so terrified.

157
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:06,960
I was truly grateful to you
that day, Dr. Ju.

158
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:13,100
But why do you keep being
so nice to me?

159
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:16,270
I feel grateful, but also guilty.

160
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:20,240
That hurts my feelings a little.

161
00:08:21,570 --> 00:08:24,880
- Pardon?
- Aren't we friends?

162
00:08:26,010 --> 00:08:28,410
Ever since we went
to that play together,

163
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:30,080
that's how I've thought of us.

164
00:08:31,380 --> 00:08:33,320
You were kind to me
before that, too.

165
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:34,890
Even before we became friends.

166
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:38,590
Without even knowing the reason,

167
00:08:38,660 --> 00:08:39,990
I feel bad
constantly troubling you...

168
00:08:41,560 --> 00:08:43,260
and taking your help...

169
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:48,030
My wife and daughter...

170
00:08:48,930 --> 00:08:52,070
passed away long ago in a car crash.

171
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:54,710
What?

172
00:08:54,940 --> 00:08:57,780
After holding the funeral in a daze,
I returned home,

173
00:08:58,540 --> 00:09:00,140
and I couldn't do a single thing.

174
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:03,050
For days, far from eating,

175
00:09:03,510 --> 00:09:05,850
I couldn't even swallow
a sip of water.

176
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:07,920
Back then,

177
00:09:08,290 --> 00:09:10,760
one of the two people who gave me...

178
00:09:11,220 --> 00:09:14,130
a reason to keep living
was you, Ms. Jo.

179
00:09:19,860 --> 00:09:23,940
I had no desire to go on,
nor any reason to,

180
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:26,840
and no matter how hard I tried,
I couldn't find one,

181
00:09:27,740 --> 00:09:30,170
so in the middle of the night,
I just wandered out.

182
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:32,680
Looking back,

183
00:09:33,180 --> 00:09:35,750
I suppose I walked out
because I was hungry.

184
00:09:37,150 --> 00:09:40,050
I simply walked
wherever my feet took me.

185
00:09:44,220 --> 00:09:47,120
I'm sorry. We're closed for the day.

186
00:09:49,460 --> 00:09:50,460
Okay.

187
00:09:51,700 --> 00:09:53,400
Wait a moment, sir.

188
00:09:55,370 --> 00:09:57,340
It looks like you haven't eaten yet,

189
00:09:58,140 --> 00:10:00,070
but we're all out of chicken today.

190
00:10:01,410 --> 00:10:03,010
Would you like some rice at least?

191
00:10:04,210 --> 00:10:06,840
No, I'm fine.

192
00:10:07,380 --> 00:10:08,380
Have some...

193
00:10:09,780 --> 00:10:11,450
warm soup and rice before you go.

194
00:10:12,980 --> 00:10:14,490
I'll get it ready right away.

195
00:10:18,690 --> 00:10:19,690
Here.

196
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:28,600
(Chief Mourner)

197
00:10:29,170 --> 00:10:30,630
Just wait a moment.

198
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:34,410
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

199
00:10:40,110 --> 00:10:41,110
Here you go.

200
00:10:47,020 --> 00:10:50,220
I run this place with my mother.

201
00:10:50,890 --> 00:10:53,590
These are just side dishes
we eat while working,

202
00:10:54,060 --> 00:10:55,290
but I think you'll like them.

203
00:10:57,600 --> 00:10:58,700
Take your time.

204
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:01,630
Yes, thank...

205
00:11:02,670 --> 00:11:03,800
Thank you for the meal.

206
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:09,270
If the soup is too bland,
you can add some salt over there.

207
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:11,640
Okay.

208
00:11:12,310 --> 00:11:14,310
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

209
00:11:45,540 --> 00:11:50,110
That day, when I tried to pay,
you wouldn't take my money.

210
00:11:53,420 --> 00:11:56,120
That was probably because
I didn't serve you chicken soup,

211
00:11:56,190 --> 00:11:57,560
so I couldn't charge you.

212
00:11:58,290 --> 00:11:59,820
I do that sometimes.

213
00:12:00,590 --> 00:12:02,160
There are days when...

214
00:12:02,390 --> 00:12:05,360
turning away a customer who comes by
weighs heavily on my mind.

215
00:12:05,700 --> 00:12:06,700
Yes.

216
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,170
You told me your chicken soup
was delicious,

217
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:11,670
apologized for being
out of ingredients,

218
00:12:11,900 --> 00:12:15,840
and asked me to please
come back again next time.

219
00:12:17,780 --> 00:12:20,210
I wanted to repay that kindness.

220
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:25,920
I wanted to keep my promise to you
when you told me to return.

221
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:28,750
So whenever I thought of it,

222
00:12:29,250 --> 00:12:32,560
I kept coming back, time and again.

223
00:12:34,930 --> 00:12:36,030
Is that so?

224
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:37,760
All I did...

225
00:12:38,230 --> 00:12:40,930
- was give you a bowl of rice.
- To me,

226
00:12:41,430 --> 00:12:43,930
the meal you gave me that day...

227
00:12:44,300 --> 00:12:46,900
was so warm and delicious.

228
00:12:48,470 --> 00:12:51,840
Stepping back out into the street
after eating that meal,

229
00:12:52,740 --> 00:12:54,780
I wondered if I could
try living again,

230
00:12:54,950 --> 00:12:57,350
and that gave me the strength
to carry on.

231
00:12:59,450 --> 00:13:00,650
You've endured...

232
00:13:01,290 --> 00:13:03,120
such a difficult time, Dr. Ju.

233
00:13:03,690 --> 00:13:06,020
It was thanks to you. Truly.

234
00:13:06,620 --> 00:13:09,390
So please don't feel bad,

235
00:13:09,660 --> 00:13:12,000
and please let me
help you this time.

236
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:16,400
You asked me to come back,
and I kept that promise to you...

237
00:13:16,700 --> 00:13:18,500
for a very long time.

238
00:13:19,400 --> 00:13:23,940
Now it's your turn
to make a promise to me.

239
00:13:28,380 --> 00:13:29,410
Promise me...

240
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:33,480
that you'll actively
pursue treatment.

241
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:39,360
All right.

242
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:41,260
Thank you.

243
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:47,460
(Consultation Room)

244
00:13:48,170 --> 00:13:49,730
What's taking so long?

245
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:53,470
She only came in for indigestion,
but she's still not out yet.

246
00:13:54,170 --> 00:13:55,740
What on earth
are they talking about?

247
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:58,240
(Consultation Room)

248
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:02,310
Did your appointment go well?

249
00:14:03,150 --> 00:14:04,250
You put on makeup.

250
00:14:09,250 --> 00:14:11,620
Is something wrong?

251
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:14,430
I'm warning you one last time.

252
00:14:14,690 --> 00:14:16,030
Don't act as if you know me.

253
00:14:16,790 --> 00:14:18,430
I don't even consider you human.

254
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:24,300
Have a good day.

255
00:14:31,310 --> 00:14:32,880
She's like a whole new person.

256
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:35,350
All dressed up, wearing makeup...

257
00:14:39,150 --> 00:14:40,150
No way.

258
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:43,320
No, it couldn't be that.

259
00:14:44,520 --> 00:14:46,090
What would Director Ju
see in her anyway?

260
00:14:47,590 --> 00:14:48,590
No, absolutely not.

261
00:15:00,170 --> 00:15:01,170
It's locked.

262
00:15:11,620 --> 00:15:12,680
Mom, it's me.

263
00:15:13,820 --> 00:15:16,550
- It's your son, Hak Sung.
- So?

264
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:18,320
The kids' mom isn't home right now,
is she?

265
00:15:19,090 --> 00:15:22,630
She's not.
She's out all the time these days.

266
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:24,530
Why do you ask?

267
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:28,870
Open the gate, please.
I brought something to give you.

268
00:15:29,900 --> 00:15:31,070
Mom.

269
00:15:39,180 --> 00:15:42,280
Is she trying to keep her distance
because of Mi Mi?

270
00:15:50,990 --> 00:15:53,260
After what you've become,
you should be hustling...

271
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:54,630
to earn even a penny more.

272
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:56,430
Why come here in broad daylight?

273
00:15:56,690 --> 00:15:57,700
Mom.

274
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:09,440
All right.

275
00:16:15,380 --> 00:16:17,080
- That's enough.
- All right.

276
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:21,150
It's abalone porridge.

277
00:16:21,650 --> 00:16:24,720
I bought the ingredients,
and Ye Ri's mom cooked it for you.

278
00:16:24,920 --> 00:16:25,920
Please eat.

279
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:33,830
Do you think doing this
will make me take you back?

280
00:16:34,370 --> 00:16:36,030
Just try a bite first.

281
00:16:36,170 --> 00:16:39,270
Think of the effort of the person
who made and brought it.

282
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:41,740
I'll leave as soon as I see you eat.

283
00:16:44,070 --> 00:16:47,210
Mrs. Choi,
why aren't you coming out?

284
00:16:47,850 --> 00:16:50,850
We're packed with customers.
Please hurry up and come out.

285
00:16:51,450 --> 00:16:53,650
What do we do about this?

286
00:16:53,950 --> 00:16:56,490
You're driving me crazy, honestly.

287
00:16:57,590 --> 00:16:58,590
I'll get going, Mom.

288
00:16:58,660 --> 00:17:01,490
You won't make it out alive
through there.

289
00:17:02,030 --> 00:17:05,030
- Go hide in my room for now.
- Okay.

290
00:17:07,230 --> 00:17:11,170
Why are you going there?
I switched rooms ages ago.

291
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:16,370
Good grief.

292
00:17:16,770 --> 00:17:19,940
- Mrs. Choi.
- I was just...

293
00:17:20,380 --> 00:17:22,110
about to head out.

294
00:17:22,180 --> 00:17:24,950
- Let's go.
- Just a second, Mrs. Choi.

295
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:26,320
What is it?

296
00:17:26,720 --> 00:17:30,490
I'll change my pants first.
Go on ahead.

297
00:17:30,750 --> 00:17:33,620
Wait, what's wrong with those pants?

298
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:36,790
I guess I lost weight...

299
00:17:36,790 --> 00:17:38,300
because things have been
tough lately.

300
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:40,060
The waist keeps slipping down.

301
00:17:41,230 --> 00:17:42,930
No, you can't.

302
00:17:44,230 --> 00:17:45,700
What do you mean?

303
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,070
Look.

304
00:17:49,170 --> 00:17:51,840
All you have to do
is fold it once like this.

305
00:17:51,910 --> 00:17:54,240
Let's hurry. You said customers
are filling up the place.

306
00:17:54,310 --> 00:17:55,310
Hurry.

307
00:17:57,510 --> 00:17:59,020
Wait, I've never seen...

308
00:17:59,580 --> 00:18:02,990
these shoes before.
Did someone come over, Mrs. Choi?

309
00:18:03,250 --> 00:18:05,120
Who would come over?

310
00:18:05,690 --> 00:18:06,890
They must be Dae Chi's.

311
00:18:07,760 --> 00:18:10,430
Dae Chi doesn't wear these.
How strange.

312
00:18:10,830 --> 00:18:12,960
Good grief!
Everything is strange to you.

313
00:18:23,710 --> 00:18:25,480
Gosh, I made it out alive.

314
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:34,080
She still keeps everything so tidy.
Nothing has changed at all.

315
00:18:35,420 --> 00:18:36,420
Right.

316
00:18:36,490 --> 00:18:38,060
This is no time
for me to be dawdling.

317
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:54,840
Who are you?

318
00:18:58,540 --> 00:18:59,580
I asked who you are.

319
00:19:02,180 --> 00:19:03,880
Thief!

320
00:19:04,380 --> 00:19:06,550
A thief! Mom! Grandma!

321
00:19:07,250 --> 00:19:08,850
I'm not a thief, kid.

322
00:19:09,350 --> 00:19:11,590
Then why are you
coming out of my mom's room?

323
00:19:11,660 --> 00:19:12,790
You're definitely a thief.

324
00:19:13,290 --> 00:19:14,290
I'm...

325
00:19:16,930 --> 00:19:18,460
You got caught trying
to rob someone's house,

326
00:19:18,530 --> 00:19:20,430
and you have the nerve
to talk back, mister?

327
00:19:20,930 --> 00:19:22,430
We're going to the police station
right now.

328
00:19:23,100 --> 00:19:24,940
Let go of me, Kang Dae Chi.

329
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:29,740
- How do you know my name?
- As for who I am...

330
00:19:30,940 --> 00:19:32,940
- I'm...
- You're...

331
00:19:34,210 --> 00:19:35,410
I'm your father.

332
00:19:35,950 --> 00:19:37,880
Kang...

333
00:19:38,220 --> 00:19:39,980
You mean you're Kang Hak Sung?

334
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:43,050
Yes, no matter
how much time has passed,

335
00:19:43,150 --> 00:19:45,790
how could you not even recognize
your own father's face?

336
00:19:52,330 --> 00:19:53,330
Get out.

337
00:19:53,830 --> 00:19:56,970
Where do you think you are?
What? Father?

338
00:19:57,630 --> 00:19:59,440
Since when did I ever have a father?

339
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:02,110
Hey, Dae Chi.
Let's let go of each other...

340
00:20:02,210 --> 00:20:04,540
and talk this through calmly, okay?

341
00:20:06,740 --> 00:20:07,950
Get out right now.

342
00:20:08,450 --> 00:20:09,450
I don't know...

343
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:12,420
what else I might do
right here if you stay.

344
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:14,080
How...

345
00:20:14,890 --> 00:20:17,090
dare you step into our house,
of all people?

346
00:20:17,590 --> 00:20:21,430
Grandma opened the door for me.
She let me in.

347
00:20:21,490 --> 00:20:23,730
I just came by
to drop something off.

348
00:20:24,130 --> 00:20:25,830
Dae Chi, sweetheart.

349
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:28,800
Did you really let him in, Grandma?
Did you?

350
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:33,340
Wait, then those shoes
by the front door earlier were...

351
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:35,870
Mrs. Choi.

352
00:20:38,010 --> 00:20:39,280
Hey, Dae Chi.

353
00:20:39,710 --> 00:20:42,550
- Let's talk for a second, okay?
- Let go of me!

354
00:20:43,650 --> 00:20:47,220
I guess you knew too.
Was I the only one who didn't know?

355
00:20:48,150 --> 00:20:49,550
How could all of you do this?

356
00:20:50,450 --> 00:20:53,290
How could you let Kang Hak Sung
into our house?

357
00:20:56,190 --> 00:20:57,890
Watch your mouth
in front of Grandma.

358
00:20:58,460 --> 00:20:59,600
Get inside right now!

359
00:21:01,230 --> 00:21:02,230
Darn it.

360
00:21:07,370 --> 00:21:08,640
Unbelievable.

361
00:21:09,310 --> 00:21:13,340
Now the whole neighborhood knows
what a dysfunctional mess we are.

362
00:21:13,680 --> 00:21:14,950
I'm utterly speechless.

363
00:21:16,550 --> 00:21:17,680
I'm sorry, Ri Ja.

364
00:21:18,780 --> 00:21:19,880
I'm sorry, Mom.

365
00:21:21,150 --> 00:21:22,320
Leave quickly...

366
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:24,820
before things get any uglier.

367
00:21:26,390 --> 00:21:27,760
Get out of our house right now,

368
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:30,730
before my sister gets here
and knocks your teeth out.

369
00:21:32,530 --> 00:21:33,560
Mi Mi.

370
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:40,800
Why are you standing here
leaving the restaurant unattended?

371
00:21:41,100 --> 00:21:42,110
Hurry up and get over there.

372
00:21:42,840 --> 00:21:43,910
Right.

373
00:21:45,140 --> 00:21:49,080
Mi Mi, let me explain
what happened here.

374
00:21:49,450 --> 00:21:50,980
You don't need to explain
anything, Mother.

375
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:53,750
Get out of my house...

376
00:21:54,350 --> 00:21:55,390
before I call the police.

377
00:21:56,020 --> 00:21:58,390
Right, I'm leaving.

378
00:22:07,330 --> 00:22:08,530
I'm going, Mom.

379
00:22:09,700 --> 00:22:11,400
Why did you bring porridge
in the first place?

380
00:22:11,670 --> 00:22:13,700
Don't you ever come back here.
Got it?

381
00:22:15,110 --> 00:22:16,110
Yes.

382
00:22:22,910 --> 00:22:24,010
What a miserable life.

383
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:28,520
Walking on eggshells
around my daughter-in-law at my age.

384
00:22:31,760 --> 00:22:32,860
Hey, Kang Dae Chi.

385
00:22:33,690 --> 00:22:34,930
Have you grown up at all?

386
00:22:36,160 --> 00:22:37,230
What about you?

387
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:39,860
I think I'm way more mature
than you are.

388
00:22:40,360 --> 00:22:43,200
Even if he had an affair
and started a whole new family,

389
00:22:43,830 --> 00:22:45,540
he's still our father, you jerk.

390
00:22:45,670 --> 00:22:46,870
What do you expect? I'm furious.

391
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:49,170
How am I supposed to act
when it's infuriating?

392
00:22:51,440 --> 00:22:52,640
When he stands there shamelessly...

393
00:22:53,540 --> 00:22:55,910
telling me, "I'm your father,"
how could I not lose my mind?

394
00:22:57,480 --> 00:22:59,350
I don't know how you feel,

395
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:02,020
but my stomach turns,
and my blood boils.

396
00:23:02,690 --> 00:23:04,550
Just hearing that man's name
makes me sick.

397
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:07,360
Hey, I feel the exact same way.

398
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:10,890
But no matter how much
we hate and resent Kang Hak Sung,

399
00:23:11,360 --> 00:23:12,560
do you think it compares to Mom?

400
00:23:14,970 --> 00:23:18,770
Do you think we're even half
as sickened and enraged as she is?

401
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:21,710
What did Mom say?

402
00:23:22,810 --> 00:23:24,710
If Grandma brought him
into our house,

403
00:23:24,710 --> 00:23:26,380
there's no way Mom
doesn't know by now.

404
00:23:26,510 --> 00:23:27,840
She hasn't said a word.

405
00:23:28,450 --> 00:23:30,680
She's so devastated and shocked...

406
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:34,380
that she won't even open her mouth,
and you know how she loves to nag.

407
00:23:36,450 --> 00:23:40,420
So stop making a scene.
Let's not make things worse for her.

408
00:23:41,860 --> 00:23:43,730
Please, just listen to me, okay?

409
00:23:44,730 --> 00:23:45,760
Whatever.

410
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:48,300
I'm not a pushover like you.

411
00:24:02,880 --> 00:24:03,880
Good morning.

412
00:24:06,420 --> 00:24:07,420
(Missing Person)

413
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:16,960
(Missing Person)

414
00:24:19,160 --> 00:24:22,030
(Jeon Dam I, Age 5, Lost in 2002)

415
00:24:27,040 --> 00:24:28,140
Good morning, CEO Jeon.

416
00:24:28,270 --> 00:24:30,440
What are you all doing
leaving these filthy flyers...

417
00:24:30,510 --> 00:24:32,080
lying around the building?

418
00:24:32,240 --> 00:24:34,040
I'm sorry.
I'll clean them up right away.

419
00:24:34,310 --> 00:24:36,550
Check every inch of the building,
inside and out,

420
00:24:36,610 --> 00:24:37,680
and get rid of all of them.

421
00:24:37,880 --> 00:24:40,080
Make sure I don't see
a single one anywhere.

422
00:24:40,480 --> 00:24:41,480
Yes, ma'am.

423
00:24:47,220 --> 00:24:48,360
(Missing Person)

424
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:56,200
CEO Jeon?

425
00:24:57,170 --> 00:24:58,200
Is everything okay?

426
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:00,000
Why are you standing out here?

427
00:25:01,300 --> 00:25:02,410
And what is that?

428
00:25:06,710 --> 00:25:08,310
Even after I warned them,

429
00:25:08,850 --> 00:25:10,610
there were flyers scattered
around the office,

430
00:25:11,280 --> 00:25:13,080
so I was just telling them
to throw them away.

431
00:25:15,290 --> 00:25:16,620
You must be getting back
from an errand.

432
00:25:18,760 --> 00:25:19,820
With Kang Da Mi?

433
00:25:21,420 --> 00:25:23,730
Yes, Head Designer Cha
had something urgent come up,

434
00:25:23,790 --> 00:25:24,960
so we went together.

435
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:33,000
Keep up the good work, then.

436
00:25:41,950 --> 00:25:42,980
Wait.

437
00:25:45,980 --> 00:25:47,380
Kang Da Mi?

438
00:25:49,290 --> 00:25:50,290
Da Mi?

439
00:25:53,120 --> 00:25:54,560
She gets on my nerves as it is,

440
00:25:55,360 --> 00:25:56,560
and now even her name is similar.

441
00:25:58,860 --> 00:26:00,760
(Missing Person)

442
00:26:00,830 --> 00:26:02,230
(Jeon Dam I, Age 5, Lost in 2002)

443
00:26:17,080 --> 00:26:18,180
No, this can't be happening.

444
00:26:18,950 --> 00:26:19,980
Not yet.

445
00:26:32,700 --> 00:26:33,860
Gang Nam...

446
00:26:35,630 --> 00:26:36,670
Dae Chi...

447
00:26:38,340 --> 00:26:39,370
My sweet daughter...

448
00:26:41,040 --> 00:26:42,040
Kids.

449
00:26:46,580 --> 00:26:48,110
Mi Mi.

450
00:26:48,750 --> 00:26:50,850
What's wrong?

451
00:26:50,850 --> 00:26:55,190
Why are you like this, Mi Mi?

452
00:26:56,290 --> 00:26:57,320
- Mother.
- Yes.

453
00:26:58,720 --> 00:27:00,220
Mother.

454
00:27:01,390 --> 00:27:02,760
What's wrong with you?

455
00:27:19,810 --> 00:27:21,640
(Mission: Mompossible)

456
00:27:37,630 --> 00:27:38,630
Ms. Cha Se Na!

457
00:27:38,700 --> 00:27:40,530
Do you have any idea
how worried I was?

458
00:27:40,900 --> 00:27:43,170
Look into someone for me.
Her name is Kang Da Mi.

459
00:27:43,370 --> 00:27:45,200
Do you see Manager Kang as a woman?

460
00:27:45,300 --> 00:27:48,710
When it comes to who I love and see,
I want to decide that for myself.

461
00:27:49,040 --> 00:27:52,140
I could live without you,

462
00:27:52,410 --> 00:27:55,780
but I can't bear to watch
our Mi Mi collapse again.

463
00:27:57,010 --> 00:27:59,020
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
